msgid "**Definition:** A policy that, after an initial premium or premiums, pays out a sum at pre-determined intervals.

For example, a policy holder may pay $10,000, and in return receive $150 each month until he dies; or $1,000 for each of 14 years or death benefits if he dies before the full term of the annuity has elapsed."
msgstr ""

# null
#: TLIFE
msgid "term life insurance policy"
msgstr ""

# null
#: TLIFE@definition
msgid "**Definition:** Life insurance under which the benefit is payable only if the insured dies during a specified period. If an insured dies during that period, the beneficiary receives the death payments. If the insured survives, the policy ends and the beneficiary receives nothing."
msgstr ""

# null
#: ULIFE
msgid "universal life insurance policy"
msgstr ""

